 holding on to it  to the extent that they begin to lose  the connection with the citizens  and therefore their usefulness comes  into question  so when it starts to fall they start to  lose control  over the planets that are in the  periphery the ones that are farthest  from the center  and as time goes on their ability to  hold on to those civilizations weakens  because this begins to happen out there  and most of the people who are really  powerful within the empire  structure are located towards the center  they would find it  very hard to believe that the empire was  falling at all  there's really no immediate effect on  their lives or the communities they live  in  so they're somewhat blind to what's  actually going on  i will cover more of this as i do the  next couple videos where i talk about  trantor  and get into the idea of psycho history  i want to do that separately i want to  look at it rather closely for a couple  of reasons  one it's interesting and also because on  reread that is the part that feels  most out of step of where we're at the  idea behind forming the foundation  it's pretty much rooted in a  technocratic ideal  which makes sense for the time obviously  at the end of world war ii  they were hoping things would be  different going forward  after the last 13 years or so after the  last year  especially it's been becoming more clear  that  an educated group of elites are probably  not going to save us  and that's not to say that the book is  no longer an interesting thought  experiment  most of what's interesting about it most  of the tension  comes from carrying the plan out  thinking about what that means  seeing how they do that and thinking  about how you might react if faced with  similar situations  so that's something that we'll look at  in future videos  for now this feels like a good place to  leave it if you have a passing interest  in the history of humanity in the  history of  empire how they come to an end i  certainly don't want to  discourage you from reading this series  if what you're hearing here sounds  interesting  i did provide links to the books in the  video description  if you're on the fence you can also find  it out there there's a bbc  version of this like a radio version  where they have actors  read different parts that's a pretty  good free introduction to the series  the one recommendation i would make and  i feel pretty strongly about this  is don't read the prequels first don't  read it in chronological order  without giving away spoilers i'll just  say that publication order  is far superior in this instance so let  me know what you think about this  empire how it stacks up against others  from popular sci-fi  franchises let me know if you have any  questions  what you're hoping to see in the apple  adaptation  and if you think that they'll be able to  pull it off please like this video if  you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already this is just the  beginning of the foundation  content i'm planning on making over the  summer thanks for watching i'll talk to  you soon

